const seedInstructions={
'chipotle-bowl':`Use the lowest-friction rice option first. Microwave rice is fine. If cooking dry rice: add 1 cup white rice and 1.5 cups water to a small pot, bring to a boil on the induction burner, cover, turn to low, cook 15 minutes, then rest 5 minutes.
Put 8 oz pre-cooked chicken in a bowl or skillet. Microwave 60-90 seconds, or warm in a skillet on medium heat for 3-5 minutes. Add a small splash of water if it looks dry.
Warm queso in a small microwave-safe cup for 20-30 seconds. Stir. If still cold, heat 10-15 seconds more.
Build the bowl in this order so it feels like Chipotle: rice on bottom, chicken, lettuce, shredded cheese, queso, then taco sauce or salsa.
Beginner cue: everything is already cooked except the rice. You are mainly reheating and assembling.
Cleanup target: one bowl, one spoon, plus either one rice pot or one microwave rice pouch.`,
'beef-rice-bowl':`If you have energy, cook 1 lb ground beef even if the recipe uses less. The extra becomes tomorrow's bowl, pasta, potato bowl, or burger-style bowl.
Start rice first. Use microwave rice, or cook dry rice in a small pot with 1 cup rice and 1.5 cups water: boil, cover, low heat 15 minutes, rest 5 minutes. Use about 2 cups cooked rice in the bowl.
Place the ground beef block in a skillet on the induction burner. Set heat to medium. Let it sit untouched for 2-3 minutes so the bottom browns.
Use a spatula to break the beef into small crumbles about dime to quarter size. Keep stirring and breaking it up for 5-8 minutes until no pink remains. If you use a thermometer, ground beef should hit 160 F.
Sprinkle taco seasoning over the beef. Add 1-2 tbsp water, stir, and cook 1-2 minutes until the seasoning coats the meat instead of looking powdery.
Microwave frozen broccoli in a covered bowl with a splash of water for 2-4 minutes. Because your microwave is weak, add 30 second rounds until hot.
Build the bowl: about 2 cups cooked rice, beef, broccoli, queso. Change the sauce when bored: taco sauce, ranch, burger sauce, or teriyaki.
Cleanup target: one skillet, one rice pot or pouch, one bowl.`,
'orange-chicken-rice':`Start rice first. Use microwave rice when tired, or cook dry rice in a small pot: 1 cup rice, 1.5 cups water, boil, cover, low heat 15 minutes, rest 5 minutes. Use about 2 cups cooked rice for the bowl.
Preheat the Ninja XL if you normally do. Put frozen orange chicken pieces in a single layer in the basket or on the tray. Do not add sauce yet.
Cook around 380-400 F for 12-16 minutes, shaking or flipping once halfway. Use the bag directions if they differ. The outside should look crisp, not pale and icy.
Warm the sauce packet in a cup of warm water or microwave it in a microwave-safe bowl for 10-20 seconds. Do not microwave a sealed packet.
Microwave frozen broccoli with a splash of water for 2-4 minutes, then add 30 second rounds until hot.
Toss about 1.5 servings of chicken with sauce, then serve over rice with broccoli on the side or mixed in.
Cleanup target: Ninja basket or tray, one rice container, one bowl.`,
'loaded-potato-beef-bowl':`Use small or medium potatoes if possible. Wash them, poke each potato 5-6 times with a fork, and microwave on a plate for 5 minutes.
Flip the potatoes carefully with a fork or towel. Microwave 3-5 minutes more. They are ready when a knife slides into the center without much resistance.
For crispier potatoes, cut the softened potatoes into rough 1 inch chunks. The exact shape does not matter. Put chunks in the Ninja XL at 400 F for 8-12 minutes.
Cook ground beef in a skillet on medium induction heat. Let it brown 2 minutes, break it into crumbles, and cook 5-8 minutes until no pink remains.
Split the potato or add chunks to a bowl. Add beef, shredded cheese, warm queso, and ranch.
Beginner cue: if the potato is hard in the middle, microwave it more. If the beef is pink, cook it more.
Cleanup target: one skillet, one plate or bowl, optional Ninja tray.`,
'chicken-bacon-ranch-wrap':`Choose the bacon path based on equipment. If you are only assembling a cold wrap, use bacon bits or pre-cooked bacon. If you are already using the skillet or Ninja to toast the wrap, raw bacon is okay because it is not adding a separate cooking tool.
Raw bacon skillet option: cook 2 slices in the skillet on medium heat for 3-5 minutes per side, until browned and crisp enough for you. Move bacon to a paper towel, pour off extra grease carefully, then use the same skillet later to toast the wrap.
Raw bacon Ninja option: cook 2 slices on the tray around 375-400 F for 6-10 minutes, checking early because bacon can go from perfect to too dark quickly.
Warm pre-cooked chicken in the microwave for 45-75 seconds, or in the same skillet on medium heat for 3-4 minutes. It only needs to become hot, not brown.
Lay the tortilla flat on a plate. Spread ranch down the center in a line, leaving about 2 inches empty at the bottom.
Add lettuce first, then chicken, bacon, and shredded cheese. Keep the pile in the center strip so the wrap can close.
Fold the bottom of the tortilla up over the filling, fold both sides inward, then roll away from you while keeping the filling tucked in.
For a crispy wrap, place it seam-side down in a dry skillet on medium heat for 1-2 minutes per side, or in the Ninja XL for 2-4 minutes until lightly browned.
Cleanup target: one plate plus optional skillet or Ninja tray.`,
'chicken-caesar-wrap':`Use pre-cooked chicken. If it is cold, microwave 45-75 seconds or warm in a skillet on medium heat for 3-4 minutes.
Lay the tortilla flat. Spread Caesar dressing down the center, leaving the edges mostly clean so it will not leak.
Add romaine or bagged lettuce, chicken, and parmesan. Keep the filling in a narrow strip instead of covering the whole tortilla.
Fold the bottom edge up, fold the left and right sides inward, then roll it tight from bottom to top.
If you want it toasted, place seam-side down in a dry skillet on medium heat for 1-2 minutes per side, or use the Ninja XL for 2-4 minutes.
Beginner cue: if the wrap bursts, use less filling next time or eat it like a folded taco. It still counts.
Cleanup target: one plate plus optional skillet or Ninja tray.`,
'burger-fries':`Start fries first because they take longest. Put frozen fries in the Ninja XL in a loose single layer. Cook around 400 F for 12-18 minutes, shaking halfway, until crisp enough for you.
For one larger burger, use about 1/2 lb ground beef. Roll it gently into a ball, then flatten into a patty about 4.5 to 5 inches wide and about 1/2 inch thick. Press a small thumb dent in the center so it does not puff up.
Heat a skillet on the induction burner to medium or medium-high. Add the patty. It should sizzle, but not smoke aggressively.
Cook 4-5 minutes on the first side. Flip once. Cook 3-5 minutes on the second side until no pink remains or the center reaches 160 F.
Add 2 slices of cheese during the last minute so it melts. If it is not melting, cover the pan for 30 seconds.
Toast the bun in the Ninja XL for 1-2 minutes if you want. Assemble with burger sauce and pickles.
Low-energy option: skip forming a patty and cook loose beef crumbles. Put them on the bun like a chopped cheese.
Cleanup target: one skillet, Ninja tray, one plate.`,
'sausage-egg-cheese':`Start with the bread. Split the English muffin or bagel and toast it in the Ninja XL for 2-4 minutes, or until the edges are lightly crisp.
Cook the sausage patty according to the package. Skillet method: medium heat, 3-4 minutes per side if pre-cooked, longer if raw. Raw sausage should be browned and reach 160 F.
For easiest eggs, make scrambled eggs. Crack 2 eggs into a bowl, add a pinch of salt if wanted, and beat with a fork until the yolks and whites are mixed.
Heat a small skillet on low-medium induction heat. Add a little butter or oil if you have it. Pour in eggs and gently push them around with a spatula for 2-4 minutes until no runny liquid remains.
Add cheese to the hot eggs or sausage so it melts. Stack muffin, sausage, egg, cheese, and top muffin.
Sunny-side option: use medium-low heat, crack eggs into the pan, cook 3-5 minutes until whites are set. Cover the pan for 30-60 seconds if the top is too runny.
Cleanup target: one skillet, one plate, one fork or spatula.`,
'yogurt-granola-bowl':`Add 1.5 cups flavored Greek yogurt to a bowl. Flavored is fine because the goal is actually eating breakfast.
Slice banana into coins about 1/4 to 1/2 inch thick. If cutting feels annoying, peel it and break it into chunks by hand.
Add banana and about 3/4 cup granola on top. Do not add granola early if you hate it soggy.
If bored, swap banana for berries, cereal, apple slices, or a spoon of peanut butter. Keep the same bowl format.
Beginner cue: this is a breakfast win even if it feels too easy to count.
Cleanup target: one bowl, one spoon, optional knife.`,
'bacon-egg-cheese-bagel':`Choose the bacon path based on equipment. Raw bacon is okay if you are already using the skillet for eggs or the Ninja for the bagel. If you do not want bacon cleanup, use pre-cooked bacon or bacon bits.
Raw bacon skillet option: cook 2 slices in the skillet on medium heat for 3-5 minutes per side, until browned and crisp enough for you. Move bacon to a paper towel, pour off extra grease carefully, then cook the eggs in the same skillet.
Raw bacon Ninja option: cook 2 slices on the tray around 375-400 F for 6-10 minutes. Check early. Bacon should be browned and crisp enough for you, not black.
Split the bagel and toast it in the Ninja XL for 2-4 minutes, or until the edges are lightly crisp.
Crack 2 eggs into a bowl and beat with a fork until the yolks and whites are mixed. Add a pinch of salt if you want.
Heat a small skillet on low-medium induction heat. Add a little butter or oil if available. Pour in eggs and gently push them around for 2-4 minutes until no runny liquid remains.
Warm pre-cooked bacon for 15-30 seconds in the microwave if it is cold. Add cheese to the hot eggs so it melts.
Assemble bagel, eggs, cheese, and bacon. If the sandwich is too tall, eat it open-faced as two halves.
Cleanup target: one skillet, one bowl, one plate.`,
'hashbrown-egg-cheese-bowl':`Start hash browns first because they take longest. Put frozen hash browns in the Ninja XL in a loose layer at about 400 F for 10-15 minutes, shaking or flipping once.
If using a sausage patty, cook it at the same time if it fits in the Ninja. If cooking in a skillet, use medium heat until browned and hot through. Raw sausage should reach 160 F.
Crack 2 eggs into a bowl and beat with a fork. For scrambled eggs, use low-medium induction heat and gently push eggs around for 2-4 minutes until no liquid remains.
Cut or break the sausage into bite-size pieces if using it. Add hash browns to a bowl, then eggs, sausage, shredded cheese, and taco sauce or salsa.
Beginner cue: hash browns are done when hot and crisp enough for you; eggs are done when they are no longer shiny and wet.
Cleanup target: Ninja tray, one skillet, one bowl.`,
'protein-cereal-bowl':`Put cereal in a bowl first.
In a separate cup, mix 1 scoop whey with 1.5 cups milk. Stir hard with a fork or shake in a covered cup for 15-20 seconds. This prevents powder clumps in the cereal bowl.
Pour the protein milk over cereal.
Add banana. Slice it if you want, or break it into chunks by hand if cutting feels annoying.
If the protein powder makes the milk too thick or sweet, use less powder next time and drink the rest as a quick side shake.
Cleanup target: one bowl, one spoon, one mixing cup.`,
'waffle-yogurt-plate':`Put frozen waffles in the Ninja XL and toast for 4-6 minutes, or until hot and crisp at the edges.
Add 1.5 cups Greek yogurt to the side of the plate or a small bowl. This is the protein part, so do not skip it unless you are pairing the waffles with a shake.
Spread 2 tbsp peanut butter on the hot waffles. It should soften and spread easier after a few seconds.
Add banana on the side. Slice it into coins or just eat it whole with the plate.
Low-energy version: waffles plus yogurt only. That is still much better than no breakfast.
Cleanup target: one plate, one spoon or butter knife.`,
'cottage-cheese-crunch-bowl':`Add 1.5 cups cottage cheese to a bowl. If the texture bothers you, use less cottage cheese and more granola at first.
Add about 1/2 cup granola right before eating so it stays crunchy.
Add banana in slices or hand-broken chunks. Drizzle honey over the top if you want it sweeter.
If you get bored of banana, swap in berries, apple slices, cereal, or a spoon of peanut butter.
Beginner cue: this is a no-cook protein bowl. There is nothing to mess up.
Cleanup target: one bowl and one spoon.`,
'turkey-egg-cheese-wrap':`Lay out the tortilla before cooking so assembly is easy while the eggs are hot.
Crack 2 eggs into a bowl and beat with a fork. Add a pinch of salt if you want.
Heat a small skillet on low-medium induction heat. Add a little butter or oil if available, then pour in eggs.
Scramble for 2-4 minutes, gently pushing eggs around until no runny liquid remains. Add shredded cheese at the end so it melts.
Put 4 turkey slices down the center of the tortilla. Add spinach, then the hot cheesy eggs.
Fold the bottom up, fold both sides inward, then roll tight. Toast seam-side down in a dry skillet for 1-2 minutes per side if you want it crisp.
Cleanup target: one skillet, one bowl, one plate.`,
'steak-tacos':`Use a whole steak and cut it yourself before cooking. Pat it dry with paper towels so it browns instead of steaming.
Find the grain: look for long muscle lines running across the steak. Cut across those lines, not parallel with them. Cutting across the grain makes the pieces easier to chew.
Slice the steak into strips about 1/4 to 1/2 inch thick and 2-3 inches long. They do not need to be perfect. If the steak is slippery, cut slower and keep your fingertips tucked back.
Season the strips with salt, taco seasoning, or both. Use enough to lightly coat the outside, not bury the meat.
Heat a skillet on the induction burner to medium-high. Let the pan heat for 2 minutes. Add a small amount of oil if the pan is not nonstick.
Add about 0.6 lb steak strips in one layer. If the pan is crowded, cook in two batches. Cook 2-3 minutes without moving, flip or stir, then cook 1-2 minutes more. Thin strips cook fast.
Doneness cue: outside browned, inside can be a little pink if you like steak that way. If you want fully done, cook another 1-2 minutes. Rest steak on a plate for 3 minutes.
Warm tortillas in the same skillet for 20-30 seconds per side. Add steak, cheese, lettuce, and taco sauce. Only add onion if you specifically want Mexican-style tacos.
Cleanup target: one cutting board, one knife, one skillet, one plate.`,
'pasta-meat-sauce':`Fill a pot about halfway with water and put it on the induction burner on high. Add salt if you want. Bring it to a boil before adding pasta.
Add 5 oz dry pasta and stir right away so it does not stick. Cook for the time on the box, usually 8-12 minutes. Taste one piece; it should be soft but not mushy.
While pasta cooks, put about 1/2 lb ground beef in a skillet on medium heat. Let it brown 2 minutes, then break it into crumbles and cook 5-8 minutes until no pink remains.
Drain pasta using a colander. If you do not want to use a colander, hold the lid slightly cracked and pour water out carefully.
Add about 3/4 cup marinara to the beef skillet and heat 2-3 minutes until bubbling gently. Add pasta to the skillet if it fits, or combine everything in the pot.
Top with parmesan. Add extra cheese or sauce if you need more calories.
Cleanup target: one pot, one skillet, one bowl. To reduce dishes, eat from the pot if you are alone and tired.`,
'protein-shake':`Add liquid first so powder does not glue itself to the bottom. Pour 2 cups milk into the blender cup.
Add 1.5 scoops whey protein. Add banana in 2-3 chunks. Add 1/2 cup oats last so they blend into the liquid.
Blend 20-40 seconds. If it sounds stuck, stop, shake the cup gently, and blend again. Do not run the blender forever if the blade is not moving.
Texture fix: if too thick, add more milk. If too thin, add more oats or half a banana.
Lowest-cleanup version: skip banana and oats, add milk plus whey to a shaker or covered cup, and shake hard for 20 seconds.
Drink it with granola, cereal, crackers, or a banana if you need more calories and the shake alone is not enough.
Cleanup target: rinse the blender cup immediately before the protein dries.`
};
const seed=seedMeals.map(r=>({id:r.id,name:r.name,cat:r.category,effort:r.effort,time:r.cookTime,serv:1,notes:r.notes,inst:seedInstructions[r.id]||'',ing:r.ingredients.map(i=>({...i,notes:i.notes||''}))}));
const seedIds=new Set(seed.map(r=>r.id));
function clone(x){return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x))}function norm(s){return String(s||'').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g,' ')}function ik(n){return norm(n)}function shopKey(n,u){return ik(n)+'|'+String(u||'').trim().toLowerCase()}function esc(s){return String(s??'').replaceAll('&','&amp;').replaceAll('<','&lt;').replaceAll('>','&gt;').replaceAll('"','&quot;').replaceAll("'",'&#039;')}function qty(n){let x=Number(n);if(Number.isNaN(x))return'';return Math.abs(x-Math.round(x))<.001?String(Math.round(x)):String(Math.round(x*100)/100)}function money(n){if(n===null||n===undefined||n==='')return'--';let x=Number(n);return Number.isFinite(x)?'$'+x.toFixed(2):'--'}function numField(v){let raw=String(v??'').trim();if(raw==='')return null;let x=Number(raw);return Number.isFinite(x)&&x>=0?x:null}function pkgPrice(m){return numField(m?.pkgPrice)}function unitNorm(s){let u=norm(s).replace(/\.$/,'').replace(/\b(cooked|dry)\b/g,'').trim();let map={'fluid ounce':'fl oz','fluid ounces':'fl oz','fl. oz':'fl oz','floz':'fl oz','fl oz':'fl oz',ounces:'oz',ounce:'oz',oz:'oz',lbs:'lb',pounds:'lb',pound:'lb',lb:'lb',cups:'cup',cup:'cup',tablespoons:'tbsp',tablespoon:'tbsp',tbsps:'tbsp',tbsp:'tbsp',teaspoons:'tsp',teaspoon:'tsp',tsps:'tsp',tsp:'tsp',counts:'count',count:'count',ct:'count',each:'count',ea:'count',slices:'count',slice:'count',servings:'count',serving:'count',pieces:'count',piece:'count',scoops:'count',scoop:'count',patties:'count',patty:'count'};return map[u]||u}function convertAmount(amount,unit){let u=unitNorm(unit);let weight={oz:1,lb:16}, volume={'fl oz':1,cup:8,tbsp:.5,tsp:1/6}, count={count:1};if(weight[u])return{kind:'weight',amount:amount*weight[u],base:'oz'};if(volume[u])return{kind:'volume',amount:amount*volume[u],base:'fl oz'};if(count[u])return{kind:'count',amount:amount,base:'count'};return null}function roughOz(amount,unit){let u=unitNorm(unit),map={oz:1,lb:16,cup:8,tbsp:.5,tsp:1/6};return map[u]?amount*map[u]:null}function packageUnitValue(unit){let u=unitNorm(unit);if(['oz','lb','count','fl oz','cup','tbsp'].includes(u))return u;return''}function pkgUnitSelect(e,val){let selected=packageUnitValue(val);return `<select class="input field-select meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="pkgUnit" required>${pkgUnits.map(u=>`<option value="${esc(u)}" ${selected===u?'selected':''}>${u?esc(u):'Choose unit'}</option>`).join('')}</select>`}
function ingField(label,html){return `<div class="field"><label>${label}</label>${html}</div>`}
function renderIngCard(k,m){const e=encodeURIComponent(k),link=m.url||searchUrl(m);return `<article class="ing-card" data-ing-key="${e}" id="ing-${e}"><div class="ing-card-head row-between"><h3>${esc(m.name)}</h3><div class="ing-card-actions"><a href="${esc(link)}" class="btn btn-secondary btn-small" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${m.url?'Open product':'Search Aldi'}</a><label class="check-label"><input class="meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="verified" type="checkbox" ${m.verified?'checked':''}> Verified</label></div></div><div class="ing-fields">${ingField('Category',`<select class="input field-select meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="type">${cats.map(c=>`<option ${m.type===c?'selected':''}>${esc(c)}</option>`).join('')}</select>`)}${ingField('Search term',`<input class="input meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="term" value="${esc(m.term||m.name)}">`)}${ingField('Product URL',`<input class="input meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="url" value="${esc(m.url||'')}" placeholder="https://www.aldi.us/...">`)}${ingField('Substitute URLs',`<input class="input meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="subs" value="${esc(m.subs||'')}" placeholder="Space-separated URLs">`)}</div><div class="ing-fields ing-fields-3">${ingField('Package price',`<input class="input meta" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" data-k="${e}" data-f="pkgPrice" value="${esc(m.pkgPrice||'')}" placeholder="5.99">`)}${ingField('Package size',`<input class="input meta" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" data-k="${e}" data-f="pkgQty" value="${esc(m.pkgQty||'')}" placeholder="16">`)}${ingField('Package unit',pkgUnitSelect(e,m.pkgUnit))}</div>${ingField('Store notes',`<input class="input meta" data-k="${e}" data-f="notes" value="${esc(m.notes||'')}" placeholder="Aisle, brand, package details">`)}${renderSubLinks(m)}</article>`}
function renderShopCard(i){const m=state.meta[i.ingKey]||{},c=state.checks[i.key]||{},got=shopHave(c),link=m.url||searchUrl(m.name||i.name),ek=encodeURIComponent(i.key),em=encodeURIComponent(i.ingKey),info=packageInfo(i),cost=info.cost,printPrice=got?'Have':cost===null?'--':money(cost),used=esc([...new Set(i.recipes)].join(', ')),flags=m.verified?'verified':'';return `<div class="shop-row ${got?'done have':''}"><div class="shop-row-line"><span class="shop-row-name">${esc(i.name)}</span><span class="shop-row-dot">·</span><span class="shop-row-meta">need ${qty(i.qty)} ${esc(i.unit)}</span><span class="shop-row-dot">·</span><span class="shop-row-cost">${cost===null?'--':money(cost)}</span>${flags?`<span class="shop-row-dot">·</span><span class="shop-row-flags">${esc(flags)}</span>`:''}<span class="shop-row-dot">·</span><span class="shop-row-meta shop-row-used">${used}</span></div><div class="shop-row-bar noPrint"><a href="${esc(link)}" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${m.url?'Open':'Search'}</a><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" data-goto-ing="${em}">Edit</button><label class="check-label"><input class="check" data-k="${ek}" data-f="have" type="checkbox" ${got?'checked':''}> Have it</label></div><div class="printRow"><span class="printName">${esc(i.name)}</span><span class="printPrice">${esc(printPrice)}</span><a class="printLink" href="${esc(link)}">${esc(link)}</a></div></div>`}
function gotoIngredient(ingKey){const k=decodeURIComponent(ingKey),m=state.meta[k];document.getElementById('ingSearch').value=m?.name||'';showView('ingredients');renderMeta();requestAnimationFrame(()=>{const el=document.querySelector('.ing-card[data-ing-key="'+ingKey+'"]');if(el){el.classList.add('ing-card-focus');setTimeout(()=>el.classList.remove('ing-card-focus'),2000);el.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'})}})}function packageInfo(i){let m=i.meta||{},price=pkgPrice(m),need=Number(i.qty)||0,pkgQty=numField(m.pkgQty),pkgUnit=packageUnitValue(m.pkgUnit),needUnit=String(i.unit||'unit').trim();if(price===null)return{cost:null,packages:0,text:'Package price not set'};if(!(pkgQty>0)||!pkgUnit)return{cost:null,packages:0,text:'Package size and unit required'};let needBase=convertAmount(need,needUnit),pkgBase=convertAmount(pkgQty,pkgUnit);if(!needBase||!pkgBase||needBase.kind!==pkgBase.kind){let roughNeed=roughOz(need,needUnit),roughPkg=roughOz(pkgQty,pkgUnit);if(roughNeed!==null&&roughPkg!==null){let packages=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(roughNeed/roughPkg));return{cost:packages*price,packages,text:`Buy ${packages} package${packages===1?'':'s'} (${money(price)} / ${qty(pkgQty)} ${pkgUnit}; approx need ${qty(need)} ${needUnit})`}}return{cost:null,packages:0,text:`Cannot convert package ${pkgUnit} to recipe unit ${needUnit}`}}let packages=Math.max(1,Math.ceil(needBase.amount/pkgBase.amount));return{cost:packages*price,packages,text:`Buy ${packages} package${packages===1?'':'s'} (${money(price)} / ${qty(pkgQty)} ${pkgUnit}; need ${qty(need)} ${needUnit})`}}function itemCost(i){return packageInfo(i).cost}function uid(){return 'r-'+Date.now().toString(36)+'-'+Math.random().toString(36).slice(2,7)}function cook(inst){let lines=String(inst||'').split('\n').map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);return lines.length?`<details class="cook"><summary>Cookware-aware steps</summary><ol>${lines.map(x=>`<li>${esc(x)}</li>`).join('')}</ol></details>`:''}
function defaultMealType(r){if(!r)return'dinner';if(r.cat==='Breakfast')return'breakfast';if(r.cat==='Fallback')return'snack';if(r.cat==='Wrap')return'lunch';return'dinner'}
function emptyMealCounts(){return{breakfast:0,lunch:0,dinner:0,snack:0}}
function mealCounts(id){return mealCountsFrom(state,id)}
function totalMealsFrom(s,id){let counts=mealCountsFrom(s,id);return Object.keys(mealTypes).reduce((sum,k)=>sum+(Number(counts[k])||0),0)}
function totalMeals(id){return totalMealsFrom(state,id)}
function setMealCount(id,type,value){let counts=mealCounts(id);counts[type]=Math.max(0,Number(value)||0);syncPlanTotals()}
function syncPlanTotals(){state.plan=state.plan||{};state.planMeals=state.planMeals||{};Object.keys(state.plan||{}).forEach(id=>{if(!state.planMeals[id])mealCounts(id)});Object.keys(state.planMeals).forEach(id=>{let total=Object.keys(mealTypes).reduce((sum,k)=>sum+(Number(state.planMeals[id][k])||0),0);if(total>0)state.plan[id]=total;else{delete state.plan[id];delete state.planMeals[id];delete state.planSlots[id]}})}
function addPlannedMeal(id){let r=state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===id),type=defaultMealType(r),counts=mealCounts(id);counts[type]=(Number(counts[type])||0)+1;syncPlanTotals()}
function subLinks(m){return String(m?.subs||'').split(/\s+/).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean)}
function renderSubLinks(m){let links=subLinks(m);return links.length?`<div class="subLinks">${links.map((u,i)=>`<a href="${esc(u)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sub ${i+1}</a>`).join('')}</div>`:''}
function targetTotals(){let totals={breakfast:0,lunch:0,dinner:0,snack:0};planned().forEach(({r})=>{let counts=mealCounts(r.id);Object.keys(mealTypes).forEach(k=>totals[k]+=Number(counts[k])||0)});return totals}
function renderTargets(){let el=document.getElementById('targetSummary');if(!el)return;let totals=targetTotals();el.innerHTML=Object.entries(mealTargets).map(([k,target])=>{let count=totals[k]||0, remaining=Math.max(0,target-count), cls=count>=target?'done':'';if(count>target)cls='over';let hint=count>target?`${count-target} over target`:remaining?`${remaining} left`:'target met';return `<div class="targetBox ${cls}"><strong>${esc(mealTypes[k])}</strong><div class="targetCount">${count}/${target}</div><div class="targetHint">${esc(hint)}</div></div>`}).join('')}
function fresh(){let s={settings:{prefix:defaultPrefix,suffix:defaultSuffix},recipes:clone(seed),plan:{'chipotle-bowl':2,'beef-rice-bowl':2,'burger-fries':1,'yogurt-granola-bowl':3,'protein-shake':2},planMeals:{'chipotle-bowl':{breakfast:0,lunch:1,dinner:1,snack:0},'beef-rice-bowl':{breakfast:0,lunch:1,dinner:1,snack:0},'burger-fries':{breakfast:0,lunch:0,dinner:1,snack:0},'yogurt-granola-bowl':{breakfast:3,lunch:0,dinner:0,snack:0},'protein-shake':{breakfast:0,lunch:0,dinner:0,snack:2}},planSlots:{},calendar:[],weekStart:getWeekStart(new Date()),meta:{},checks:{},starterVersion:STARTER_VERSION};hydrate(s);syncCalendarFromPlan(s);return s}
function syncStarterRecipes(s=state,replace=false){let custom=(s.recipes||[]).filter(r=>!seedIds.has(r.id));let existing=new Map((s.recipes||[]).map(r=>[r.id,r]));s.recipes=[...clone(seed).map(r=>{let old=existing.get(r.id);if(!old)return r;if(replace&&!old.userModified)return r;return old}),...custom];s.starterVersion=STARTER_VERSION;hydrate(s)}
let state=(()=>{try{let s=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));if(!s||!Array.isArray(s.recipes))throw 0;s.settings=s.settings||{prefix:defaultPrefix,suffix:defaultSuffix};s.meta=s.meta||{};s.plan=s.plan||{};s.planMeals=s.planMeals||{};s.planSlots=s.planSlots||{};s.checks=s.checks||{};s.calendar=s.calendar||[];s.weekStart=s.weekStart||getWeekStart(new Date());if(s.starterVersion!==STARTER_VERSION)syncStarterRecipes(s,false);hydrate(s);migrateChecks();return s}catch{return fresh()}})();
function emptyMeta(name,type='Other'){return{name,type,term:name,url:'',subs:'',price:'',pkgPrice:'',pkgQty:'',pkgUnit:'',notes:'',verified:false}}
function hydrate(s=state){s.recipes.forEach(r=>(r.ing||[]).forEach(i=>{let k=ik(i.name);if(!k)return;s.meta[k]=s.meta[k]||emptyMeta(i.name,i.type||'Other');s.meta[k].name=s.meta[k].name||i.name;s.meta[k].type=s.meta[k].type||i.type||'Other';s.meta[k].term=s.meta[k].term||i.name;if(s.meta[k].subs===undefined)s.meta[k].subs='';if(s.meta[k].price===undefined)s.meta[k].price='';if(s.meta[k].pkgPrice===undefined)s.meta[k].pkgPrice='';if(s.meta[k].pkgQty===undefined)s.meta[k].pkgQty='';if(s.meta[k].pkgUnit===undefined)s.meta[k].pkgUnit='';else{let pu=packageUnitValue(s.meta[k].pkgUnit);if(pu)s.meta[k].pkgUnit=pu}}))}
function save(){syncPlanTotals();hydrate();pruneChecks();localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(state));renderExport()}
function searchUrl(m){let t=typeof m==='string'?m:(m.term||m.name||'');return (state.settings.prefix||defaultPrefix)+encodeURIComponent(t)+(state.settings.suffix||'')}
function planned(){return plannedFrom(state)}
function shopping(){hydrate();let m=new Map();planned().forEach(({r,c})=>(r.ing||[]).forEach(i=>{let key=shopKey(i.name,i.unit), meta=state.meta[ik(i.name)]||{}, old=m.get(key)||{key,ingKey:ik(i.name),name:i.name,unit:i.unit||'',qty:0,type:meta.type||i.type||'Other',recipes:[],notes:[],meta};old.qty+=(Number(i.qty)||0)*c;old.recipes.push(r.name+' x'+c);if(i.notes&&!old.notes.includes(i.notes))old.notes.push(i.notes);old.meta=meta;old.type=meta.type||old.type;m.set(key,old)}));return [...m.values()].sort((a,b)=>(a.type||'').localeCompare(b.type||'')||a.name.localeCompare(b.name))}
function shopHave(c){return!!(c&&(c.have||c.bought))}
function migrateChecks(){Object.values(state.checks||{}).forEach(c=>{if(c.bought){c.have=c.have||c.bought;delete c.bought}})}
function pruneChecks(){migrateChecks();let valid=new Set(shopping().map(i=>i.key));Object.keys(state.checks||{}).forEach(k=>{if(!valid.has(k))delete state.checks[k]})}
function groups(){let g={};shopping().forEach(i=>{(g[i.type||'Other']??=[]).push(i)});let out={};cats.forEach(c=>{if(g[c])out[c]=g[c]});Object.keys(g).sort().forEach(c=>{if(!out[c])out[c]=g[c]});return out}
function match(r,q){if(!q)return true;return [r.name,r.cat,r.effort,r.notes,r.inst,...(r.ing||[]).map(i=>i.name+' '+i.type+' '+i.notes)].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q)}
function filterValue(id){let el=document.getElementById(id);return el?el.value:''}
function matchesDefaultMeal(r,type){return !type||defaultMealType(r)===type}
function matchesPlannedMeal(r,type){return !type||(mealCounts(r.id)[type]||0)>0}
function recipeGrid(rs,planMode,emptyText){return rs.length?rs.map(r=>card(r,planMode)).join(''):`<p class="muted">${esc(emptyText)}</p>`}
function card(r,planMode=false){let c=Number(state.plan[r.id]||0);return `<article class="recipe"><h3>${esc(r.name)}</h3><span class="pill">${esc(r.cat)}</span><span class="pill gray">${esc(r.effort)} effort</span><span class="pill gray">${esc(r.time)}</span>${c?`<span class="pill ok">planned x${c}</span>`:''}<p class="muted">${esc(r.notes||'')}</p>${cook(r.inst)}<ul>${(r.ing||[]).slice(0,6).map(i=>`<li>${esc(i.name)} - ${qty(i.qty)} ${esc(i.unit)}</li>`).join('')}${(r.ing||[]).length>6?'<li>+ more</li>':''}</ul><div class="actions">${planMode?`<button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-small" data-add="${esc(r.id)}">Add Meal</button>`:''}<button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary btn-small" data-edit="${esc(r.id)}">Edit</button><button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary btn-small" data-dup="${esc(r.id)}">Duplicate</button></div></article>`}
function renderPlan(){renderPlanSummary();renderCalendar();renderTargets();let selectedType=filterValue('plannedMealFilter'),p=planned().filter(({r})=>matchesPlannedMeal(r,selectedType)),empty=selectedType?`No ${mealTypes[selectedType].toLowerCase()} recipes selected yet.`:'No recipes selected yet.';document.getElementById('planned').innerHTML=p.length?`<div class="wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th>Recipe</th><th>Breakfast</th><th>Lunch</th><th>Dinner</th><th>Snacks</th><th>Total</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>${p.map(({r,c})=>{let counts=mealCounts(r.id);return `<tr><td><b>${esc(r.name)}</b><br><span class="muted">${esc(r.cat)} / ${esc(r.effort)}</span></td>${Object.keys(mealTypes).map(k=>`<td><input class="input mealCountInput" data-meal-count="${esc(r.id)}" data-kind="${k}" type="number" min="0" value="${counts[k]||0}"></td>`).join('')}<td><b class="num">${c}</b></td><td><button type="button" class="btn btn-red btn-small" data-remove="${esc(r.id)}">Remove</button></td></tr>`}).join('')}</tbody></table></div>`:`<p class="muted">${esc(empty)}</p>`;let q=document.getElementById('planSearch').value.toLowerCase(),planType=filterValue('planMealFilter'),planMatches=state.recipes.filter(r=>match(r,q)&&matchesDefaultMeal(r,planType));document.getElementById('planRecipes').innerHTML=recipeGrid(planMatches,true,'No recipes match those filters.')}
function renderRecipes(){let q=document.getElementById('recipeSearch').value.toLowerCase(),type=filterValue('recipeMealFilter'),matches=state.recipes.filter(r=>match(r,q)&&matchesDefaultMeal(r,type));document.getElementById('recipeList').innerHTML=recipeGrid(matches,false,'No recipes match those filters.')}
function renderMeta(){hydrate();document.getElementById('searchPrefix').value=state.settings.prefix||defaultPrefix;document.getElementById('searchSuffix').value=state.settings.suffix||defaultSuffix;let q=document.getElementById('ingSearch').value.toLowerCase();let rows=Object.entries(state.meta).filter(([k,m])=>!q||[m.name,m.type,m.term,m.url,m.subs,m.pkgPrice,m.pkgQty,m.pkgUnit,m.notes].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q)).sort((a,b)=>(a[1].type||'').localeCompare(b[1].type||'')||a[1].name.localeCompare(b[1].name));document.getElementById('ingRows').innerHTML=rows.length?rows.map(([k,m])=>renderIngCard(k,m)).join(''):'<p class="muted" style="padding:0 20px 20px">No ingredients match your search.</p>'}
function renderShop(){let g=groups(), el=document.getElementById('shopList');if(!Object.keys(g).length){el.innerHTML='<div class="card"><p class="muted">No shopping list yet. Add recipes first.</p></div>';return}let all=shopping(), total=all.reduce((sum,i)=>sum+(itemCost(i)||0),0), buyTotal=all.reduce((sum,i)=>sum+(shopHave(state.checks[i.key])?0:(itemCost(i)||0)),0), priced=all.filter(i=>pkgPrice(i.meta)!==null).length;let summary=`<div class="shopTotal"><div><strong>Estimated weekly ingredients</strong><div class="targetHint">${priced}/${all.length} items have package prices saved</div></div><div><span class="muted">All planned:</span> <span class="money">${money(total)}</span></div><div><span class="muted">To buy:</span> <span class="money">${money(buyTotal)}</span></div></div>`;el.innerHTML=summary+Object.entries(g).map(([cat,items])=>`<div class="card"><h3>${esc(cat)}</h3><div class="shop-list">${items.map(i=>renderShopCard(i)).join('')}</div></div>`).join('')}
let recipeDirty=false;
function fill(r){document.getElementById('rid').value=r?.id||'';document.getElementById('rname').value=r?.name||'';document.getElementById('rcat').value=r?.cat||'Rice Bowl';document.getElementById('reffort').value=r?.effort||'Low';document.getElementById('rtime').value=r?.time||'';document.getElementById('rserv').value=r?.serv||1;document.getElementById('rnotes').value=r?.notes||'';document.getElementById('rinst').value=r?.inst||'';document.getElementById('rings').value=r?(r.ing||[]).map(i=>`${i.name} | ${i.qty??''} | ${i.unit||''} | ${i.type||'Other'} | ${i.notes||''}`).join('\n'):'';document.getElementById('editTitle').textContent=r?'Edit Recipe: '+r.name:'Add / Edit Recipe';recipeDirty=false}
function parseIng(t){return String(t||'').split('\n').map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean).map(line=>{let p=line.split('|').map(x=>x.trim());return{name:p[0]||'Unnamed ingredient',qty:Number(p[1])||0,unit:p[2]||'',type:p[3]||'Other',notes:p.slice(4).join(' | ')||''}})}
function readRecipeDraft(silent=false){let id=document.getElementById('rid').value||uid(), name=document.getElementById('rname').value.trim();if(!name){if(!silent)alert('Recipe name is required.');return null}let existing=state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===id)||{};return{id,name,cat:document.getElementById('rcat').value,effort:document.getElementById('reffort').value,time:document.getElementById('rtime').value.trim(),serv:Number(document.getElementById('rserv').value)||1,notes:document.getElementById('rnotes').value.trim(),inst:document.getElementById('rinst').value.trim(),ing:parseIng(document.getElementById('rings').value),userModified:true,createdAt:existing.createdAt||new Date().toISOString(),updatedAt:new Date().toISOString()}}
function upsertRecipe(r){let idx=state.recipes.findIndex(x=>x.id===r.id);idx>=0?state.recipes[idx]=r:state.recipes.push(r)}
function commitRecipeDraft(){if(!recipeDirty)return false;if(!document.getElementById('rname').value.trim())return false;let r=readRecipeDraft(true);if(!r)return false;upsertRecipe(r);recipeDirty=false;save();fill(r);return true}
function saveRecipe(){let r=readRecipeDraft(false);if(!r)return;upsertRecipe(r);recipeDirty=false;save();renderAll();fill(r)}
function recipeSlug(name){return norm(name).replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g,'').slice(0,60)||uid()}
function uniqueRecipeId(base,keepId=''){let id=base||uid(),used=new Set(state.recipes.map(r=>r.id).filter(x=>x!==keepId));if(!used.has(id))return id;let n=2;while(used.has(`${id}-${n}`))n++;return `${id}-${n}`}
function recipeImportFormat(){return JSON.stringify({recipes:[{id:'chicken-queso-rice-bowl',name:'Chicken Queso Rice Bowl',category:'Rice Bowl',effort:'Low',cookTime:'20 min',baseServings:1,notes:'Short note shown on recipe cards.',instructions:'Cook rice. Warm chicken. Add queso and toppings.',ingredients:[{name:'White rice',quantity:2,unit:'cup cooked',type:'Carb',notes:'microwave rice is fine'},{name:'Pre-cooked chicken',quantity:8,unit:'oz',type:'Protein'},{name:'Queso',quantity:0.33,unit:'cup',type:'Sauce/Condiment'}]}]},null,2)}
function recipeExportShape(r){return{id:r.id,name:r.name,category:r.cat,effort:r.effort,cookTime:r.time,baseServings:r.serv,notes:r.notes||'',instructions:r.inst||'',ingredients:(r.ing||[]).map(i=>({name:i.name,quantity:Number(i.qty)||0,unit:i.unit||'',type:i.type||'Other',notes:i.notes||''}))}}
function recipesJson(){return JSON.stringify({recipes:state.recipes.map(recipeExportShape)},null,2)}
function normalizeIngredient(i){if(typeof i==='string')return parseIng(i)[0]||null;if(!i||typeof i!=='object')return null;let name=String(i.name||i.ingredient||'').trim();if(!name)return null;return{name,qty:Number(i.qty??i.quantity??i.amount) || 0,unit:String(i.unit||i.units||'').trim(),type:String(i.type||i.category||'Other').trim()||'Other',notes:String(i.notes||i.note||'').trim()}}
function normalizeRecipe(r){if(!r||typeof r!=='object')throw Error('Each recipe must be an object.');let name=String(r.name||r.title||'').trim();if(!name)throw Error('Every recipe needs a name.');let existingId=String(r.id||'').trim(),existing=state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===existingId)||{};let id=existingId||uniqueRecipeId(recipeSlug(name));let ingredients=(r.ing||r.ingredients||[]).map(normalizeIngredient).filter(Boolean);return{id,name,cat:String(r.cat||r.category||'Other').trim()||'Other',effort:String(r.effort||'Low').trim()||'Low',time:String(r.time||r.cookTime||r.cook_time||'').trim(),serv:Number(r.serv??r.baseServings??r.servings) || 1,notes:String(r.notes||r.description||'').trim(),inst:String(r.inst||r.instructions||r.steps||'').trim(),ing:ingredients,userModified:true,createdAt:existing.createdAt||new Date().toISOString(),updatedAt:new Date().toISOString()}}
function importRecipes(){let status=document.getElementById('recipeImportStatus');try{let raw=document.getElementById('recipeImportBox').value.trim();if(!raw)throw Error('Paste recipe JSON first.');let data=JSON.parse(raw),items=Array.isArray(data)?data:data.recipes;if(!Array.isArray(items))throw Error('Use an array of recipes or an object with a recipes array.');let added=0,updated=0;items.forEach(item=>{let r=normalizeRecipe(item),exists=state.recipes.some(x=>x.id===r.id);upsertRecipe(r);exists?updated++:added++});hydrate();save();renderAll();status.textContent=`Imported ${added} new recipe${added===1?'':'s'} and updated ${updated}.`;document.getElementById('recipeImportBox').value=''}catch(err){status.textContent='Recipe import failed: '+err.message}}
function md(){let lines=['# Takeout-at-Home Meal Plan Export','Generated: '+new Date().toLocaleString(),'','## Weekly Targets'];let totals=targetTotals();Object.entries(mealTargets).forEach(([k,target])=>lines.push(`- ${mealTypes[k]}: ${totals[k]||0}/${target}`));lines.push('','## Planned Recipes');let p=planned();if(!p.length)lines.push('- [none]');p.forEach(({r,c})=>{let split=Object.entries(mealCounts(r.id)).filter(([,n])=>n>0).map(([k,n])=>`${mealTypes[k]} ${n}`).join(', ');lines.push(`- ${r.name}: ${c} meal(s) (${split}) - ${r.cat}, ${r.effort}, ${r.time}`)});lines.push('','## Shopping List');let all=shopping(), total=all.reduce((sum,i)=>sum+(itemCost(i)||0),0), buyTotal=all.reduce((sum,i)=>sum+(shopHave(state.checks[i.key])?0:(itemCost(i)||0)),0);lines.push(`Estimated all planned: ${money(total)}`);lines.push(`Estimated to buy: ${money(buyTotal)}`);let g=groups();if(!Object.keys(g).length)lines.push('- [none]');Object.entries(g).forEach(([cat,items])=>{lines.push('',`### ${cat}`);items.forEach(i=>{let m=state.meta[i.ingKey]||{}, c=state.checks[i.key]||{}, marks=[], info=packageInfo(i), cost=info.cost, price=pkgPrice(m);if(shopHave(c))marks.push('have');if(m.verified)marks.push('Aldi verified');lines.push(`- Need ${qty(i.qty)} ${i.unit} ${i.name}${marks.length?' ('+marks.join(', ')+')':''}`);if(price!==null)lines.push(`  - Package: ${info.text}; est line cost ${money(cost)}`);lines.push(`  - Used by: ${[...new Set(i.recipes)].join(', ')}`);let notes=[m.notes,...i.notes].filter(Boolean).join('; ');if(notes)lines.push(`  - Notes: ${notes}`);lines.push(`  - Link/Search: ${m.url||searchUrl(m)}`);subLinks(m).forEach((u,idx)=>lines.push(`  - Substitute ${idx+1}: ${u}`))})});lines.push('','## Recipe Details');p.forEach(({r})=>{lines.push('',`### ${r.name}`,`- Notes: ${r.notes||''}`,`- Instructions: ${r.inst||''}`,'- Ingredients:');(r.ing||[]).forEach(i=>lines.push(`  - ${qty(i.qty)} ${i.unit} ${i.name} [${i.type}]${i.notes?' - '+i.notes:''}`))});return lines.join('\n')}
function renderExport(){let el=document.getElementById('exportBox');if(el)el.textContent=md();let fmt=document.getElementById('recipeFormatBox');if(fmt)fmt.textContent=recipeImportFormat()}
function download(fn,text,type='text/plain;charset=utf-8'){let b=new Blob([text],{type}),u=URL.createObjectURL(b),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=u;a.download=fn;document.body.appendChild(a);a.click();setTimeout(()=>{URL.revokeObjectURL(u);a.remove()},500)}
async function copy(text){try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);alert('Copied.')}catch{let t=document.createElement('textarea');t.value=text;document.body.appendChild(t);t.select();document.execCommand('copy');t.remove();alert('Copied.')}}
function renderAll(){renderPlan();renderRecipes();renderMeta();renderShop();renderExport();updateSidebarFoot()}
document.querySelectorAll('[data-view]').forEach(btn=>{btn.addEventListener('click',()=>{commitRecipeDraft();showView(btn.dataset.view)})});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{let t=e.target;if(t.closest('[data-view]')&&t.closest('.nav-list, .bottomnav'))return;if(t.dataset.calAdd){openCalendarPicker(t.dataset.calAdd);return}if(t.dataset.calRemove){removeCalendarSlot(t.dataset.calRemove);save();return renderAll()}if(t.id==='cal-pick-cancel'){document.getElementById('cal-dialog')?.close();return}if(t.id==='cal-pick-confirm'){const recipeId=document.getElementById('cal-pick-recipe')?.value,mealType=document.getElementById('cal-pick-type')?.value;if(pendingCalDate&&recipeId){addCalendarMeal(pendingCalDate,mealType,recipeId);save();renderAll()}document.getElementById('cal-dialog')?.close();return}if(t.id==='weekPrev'){shiftWeek(-1);save();return renderAll()}if(t.id==='weekNext'){shiftWeek(1);save();return renderAll()}if(t.id==='weekToday'){state.weekStart=getWeekStart(new Date());save();return renderAll()}if(t.id==='syncCalendar'){syncCalendarFromPlan();save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.gotoIng){gotoIngredient(t.dataset.gotoIng);return}if(t.dataset.add){addPlannedMeal(t.dataset.add);save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.plus){addPlannedMeal(t.dataset.plus);save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.minus){let counts=mealCounts(t.dataset.minus),type=defaultMealType(state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===t.dataset.minus));counts[type]=Math.max(0,(Number(counts[type])||0)-1);syncPlanTotals();save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.remove){const rid=t.dataset.remove;delete state.plan[rid];delete state.planMeals[rid];delete state.planSlots[rid];state.calendar=(state.calendar||[]).filter(s=>s.recipeId!==rid);save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.edit){commitRecipeDraft();let r=state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===t.dataset.edit);fill(r);tab('recipes');scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});return}if(t.dataset.dup){let r=clone(state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===t.dataset.dup));r.id=uid();r.name+=' Copy';r.userModified=true;state.recipes.push(r);save();renderAll();fill(r);tab('recipes');return}if(t.id==='saveRecipe')return saveRecipe();if(t.id==='newRecipe'){commitRecipeDraft();return fill(null)}if(t.id==='deleteRecipe'){let id=document.getElementById('rid').value;if(!id)return fill(null);let r=state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===id);if(r&&confirm('Delete '+r.name+'?')){state.recipes=state.recipes.filter(x=>x.id!==id);delete state.plan[id];delete state.planMeals[id];delete state.planSlots[id];state.calendar=(state.calendar||[]).filter(s=>s.recipeId!==id);recipeDirty=false;save();renderAll();fill(null)}return}if(t.id==='openShopping'){commitRecipeDraft();return tab('shopping')}if(t.id==='clearPlan'&&confirm('Clear weekly plan?')){state.plan={};state.planMeals={};state.planSlots={};state.calendar=[];state.checks={};save();return renderAll()}if(t.id==='saveSearch'){state.settings.prefix=document.getElementById('searchPrefix').value.trim();state.settings.suffix=document.getElementById('searchSuffix').value.trim();save();renderAll();alert('Search settings saved.');return}if(t.id==='resetSearch'){state.settings.prefix=defaultPrefix;state.settings.suffix=defaultSuffix;save();renderAll();return}if(t.id==='copyList'||t.id==='copyExport')return copy(md());if(t.id==='downloadList'||t.id==='downloadExport')return download('takeout-at-home-shopping-list.txt',md());if(t.id==='downloadJson')return download('takeout-at-home-app-backup.json',JSON.stringify(state,null,2),'application/json;charset=utf-8');if(t.id==='copyRecipeFormat')return copy(recipeImportFormat());if(t.id==='downloadRecipeFormat')return download('recipe-import-format.json',recipeImportFormat(),'application/json;charset=utf-8');if(t.id==='downloadRecipesJson')return download('mealplan-recipes.json',recipesJson(),'application/json;charset=utf-8');if(t.id==='importRecipesJson')return importRecipes();if(t.id==='clearChecks'){state.checks={};save();return renderShop()}if(t.id==='importJson'){let s=document.getElementById('backupStatus');try{let data=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('importBox').value);if(!Array.isArray(data.recipes))throw Error('Missing recipes array');state=data;state.settings=state.settings||{prefix:defaultPrefix,suffix:defaultSuffix};state.meta=state.meta||{};state.plan=state.plan||{};state.planMeals=state.planMeals||{};state.planSlots=state.planSlots||{};state.checks=state.checks||{};state.calendar=state.calendar||[];state.weekStart=state.weekStart||getWeekStart(new Date());hydrate();syncPlanTotals();save();renderAll();s.textContent='Imported successfully.'}catch(err){s.textContent='Import failed: '+err.message}return}if(t.id==='refreshStarter'&&confirm('Refresh starter recipes that you have not edited? Edited recipes and custom recipes will be kept.')){syncStarterRecipes(state,true);save();renderAll();document.getElementById('backupStatus').textContent='Starter recipes refreshed. Edited recipes were kept.';return}if(t.id==='resetApp'&&confirm('Reset to starter data?')){state=fresh();recipeDirty=false;save();renderAll();return}});
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{let t=e.target;if(recipeFieldIds.has(t.id)){recipeDirty=true;return}if(t.id==='planSearch')renderPlan();if(t.id==='recipeSearch')renderRecipes();if(t.id==='ingSearch')renderMeta();if(t.dataset.mealCount){setMealCount(t.dataset.mealCount,t.dataset.kind,t.value);syncCalendarFromPlan();save();return renderAll()}if(t.dataset.count){setMealCount(t.dataset.count,defaultMealType(state.recipes.find(x=>x.id===t.dataset.count)),t.value);save();return renderAll()}if(t.classList.contains('meta')){let k=decodeURIComponent(t.dataset.k),f=t.dataset.f;state.meta[k]=state.meta[k]||emptyMeta(k);state.meta[k][f]=t.type==='checkbox'?t.checked:t.value;save();return}});
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{let t=e.target;if(recipeFieldIds.has(t.id)){recipeDirty=true;return}if(t.id==='plannedMealFilter'||t.id==='planMealFilter')return renderPlan();if(t.id==='recipeMealFilter')return renderRecipes();if(t.dataset.meal){let counts=mealCounts(t.dataset.meal),total=totalMeals(t.dataset.meal);Object.keys(mealTypes).forEach(k=>counts[k]=0);counts[t.value]=total;syncPlanTotals();save();return renderAll()}if(t.classList.contains('check')){let k=decodeURIComponent(t.dataset.k),f=t.dataset.f;state.checks[k]=state.checks[k]||{};state.checks[k][f]=t.checked;save();renderShop()}if(t.classList.contains('meta')){let k=decodeURIComponent(t.dataset.k),f=t.dataset.f;state.meta[k]=state.meta[k]||emptyMeta(k);state.meta[k][f]=t.type==='checkbox'?t.checked:t.value;save();renderShop()}});
if(calendarSlotCount(state)<plannedMealSlotCount(state)){syncCalendarFromPlan(state);try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(state))}catch(e){}}
try{const saved=localStorage.getItem(VIEW_KEY);if(saved&&VIEWS[saved])showView(saved)}catch(e){}
renderAll();
